Description of the hierachy

- CCSL_ctx
	Definition of constants and sets used in all machines (Clocks, integers)

- "operator"_ctx
	Definition of constants specific to some operator (e.g. "b" in precedence)
	
- CCSLgeneric
	Specification of the construction of a valid trace using CCSL formulas
	Schedule add to chi and delta the first element without image based
	on the parameter clock_set (valuation of ticks for each clock)

- CCSL"operator"
	Refines generic
	Sees "operator"_ctx (or CCSLctx if no particular constants)
	Add contraints on Schedule to allow the new chi and delta to 
		respect the formula of the operator
	

- ASTD"operator"
	Refines CCSL"operator" 
		-> Proof obligation showing "concrete guard => abstract guard"
	If needed a counter or buffer is added and it is updated according to the table of update
		a gluing invariant is also added to link the counter or buffer to chi and delta
	A theorem to add the proof of "abstract guard => concrete guard"